{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ReGspdjBUsCP8ETrCnNxnp","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets (sum across all states)\ntotals = fact.aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()\n).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get total US population (where NAME = \"United States\")\ndenom = (ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\")\n         .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n         .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and compute the metric\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(denom, totals.k == denom.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / denom.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see:\n- The farmers_markets table has a row for each state with the count of farmers markets\n- The census_population table has rows for different levels of aggregation (SUMLEV column). The first row (SUMLEV=10) is the entire United States with NAME=\"United States\" and POPESTIMATE2025=341784857\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Sum total farmers markets from the farmers_markets table\n2. Get the total U.S. population from the census_population table where NAME=\"United States\" and POPESTIMATE2025 is the relevant column\n3. Calculate (total_farmers_markets / population) * 100000\n\nLet me create a build script that reads both sources and creates this metric. According to the skill, I should use a single build script that reads both sources and joins them (or in this case, gets a single row from each).","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script to compute the metric by joining both sources:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ReGspdjBUsCP8ETrCnNxnp","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read both sources\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Get total farmers markets (sum across all states)\ntotals = fact.aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()\n).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get total US population (where NAME = \"United States\")\ndenom = (ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\")\n         .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n         .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and compute the metric\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(denom, totals.k == denom.k)\n    .mutate(markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / denom.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":779,"cacheRead":19139,"cacheWrite":2502,"totalTokens":22434,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0038950000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0019139,"cacheWrite":0.0031275,"total":0.0089504},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":205},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915071121,"responseId":"msg_011Ce787qDpSBtyjG48VFDpw","rawStopReason":"tool_use"}}
